## 7. API behavior to reproduce

### 7.1 Agreement templates
Recommended endpoints:
- `GET /agreement-templates`
- `GET /agreement-templates/:id`
- `POST /agreement-templates`
- `PATCH /agreement-templates/:id`
- `POST /agreement-templates/:id/archive`

Behavior:
- create templates with version 1
- if economic config changes on an in-use template, fork/version it
- archive instead of hard-removing in normal workflows

### 7.2 Merchant agreements
Recommended endpoints:
- `GET /merchant-agreements`
- `GET /merchant-agreements/approved?merchantId=...`
- `GET /merchant-agreements/:id`
- `POST /merchant-agreements`
- `POST /merchant-agreements/:id/submit`
- `POST /merchant-agreements/:id/approve`
- `POST /merchant-agreements/:id/reject`
- `DELETE /merchant-agreements/:id`
- `POST /merchant-agreements/:id/archive`

Behavior:
- create as `pending`
- approve/reject explicitly
- return only approved active records for order entry
- archive instead of delete when referenced by orders

### 7.3 Orders
Recommended endpoints:
- `GET /orders`
- `GET /orders/incoming`
- `GET /orders/outgoing`
- `GET /orders/:id`
- `POST /orders`
- `PATCH /orders/:id`
- `DELETE /orders/:id`
- `POST /orders/:id/cancel`

Behavior:
- validate agreement status and merchant ownership on create
- store frozen agreement snapshot
- compute and persist net profit at create time
- allow hard delete only for drafts
- use cancel/archive for non-draft records

